= Paek Nam-un

Paek Nam-un was an economist and economic historian. During his studies in Japan in the 1920s, he encountered Marxism and consequently became a communist. He later returned home and took up a teaching position, conducting research on the economic history of the Korean Peninsula. In 1938, he left teaching and engaged in socialist activities, and as a result was imprisoned by the Japanese colonial authorities in 1940. After Japan surrendered in August 1945, Paek Nam-un was released.

